For the instantiated `main` defaults (`ALLOW_BYPASS=1`, `DEPTH>0`), these invariants form a one-step inductive proof after a clocked reset. Declare and assert them in `main`. Place `lemma_4` inside a generate loop with `genvar i` ranging from `0` to `DEPTH-1`, and assert every generated instance. The syntax follows IEEE 1800’s property and concurrent-assertion constructs. ([rfsoc.mit.edu](https://rfsoc.mit.edu/6S965/_static/F25/documentation/1800-2017.pdf?utm_source=openai))

**Parameter caveat:** The target property is **false** for `ALLOW_BYPASS=0` without input restrictions. An empty `pop` compares `data_out=0` against potentially uninitialized reference data. Also, an empty simultaneous `push`/`pop` raises `error` but advances the DUT’s `tail`, which can corrupt a later valid read. No sound lemmas can prove that configuration’s property as written.

<json>
{
  "lemmas": [
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (size == fv_env.fifo_size && size <= DEPTH); endproperty",
      "explanation": "The DUT and reference occupancy start at zero and make matching changes for every accepted operation. This connects the property's fifo_size guard to the DUT's empty flag."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_2; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (dut.head < DEPTH && dut.tail < DEPTH && fv_env.ref_fifo_head < DEPTH && fv_env.ref_fifo_tail < DEPTH); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Reset initializes every pointer to zero, and subsequent pointer updates wrap modulo DEPTH. The bounds make indexed buffer comparisons well-defined."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_3; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (dut.tail == ((dut.head + size) % DEPTH) && fv_env.ref_fifo_tail == ((fv_env.ref_fifo_head + fv_env.fifo_size) % DEPTH)); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Each tail marks the slot after its occupied entries. This identifies the corresponding slots written by a push, including a simultaneous push and pop at full occupancy."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_4; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (size > i) |-> (dut.buffer[(dut.head + i) % DEPTH] == fv_env.ref_fifo[(fv_env.ref_fifo_head + i) % DEPTH]); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Generate this property for every i from 0 through DEPTH-1. It equates occupied entries by logical FIFO position, rather than physical address; that distinction is essential because an empty bypass advances the reference pointers but not the DUT pointers. Together with the preceding invariants, it is preserved by push, pop, and simultaneous operations. Its i=0 instance supplies the data comparison needed by the target property."
    }
  ]
}
</json>

For the default `main` configuration (`ALLOW_BYPASS=1`), the useful strengthening is **occupancy agreement, pointer alignment, and data agreement at every occupied queue position**. These lemmas assume `DEPTH > 0` and that reset has occurred. Declare them in `main`, where both instances are visible; place `lemma_4` inside a `for (genvar i = 0; i < DEPTH; i++)` generate block and assert every instance. Each generated `i` is an elaboration-time constant. ([fpga.mit.edu](https://fpga.mit.edu/6205/_static/F25/documentation/1800-2017.pdf))

**Limitation:** No sound lemmas can prove `prop` for `ALLOW_BYPASS=0` as written. Fill the FIFO with ones, drain it, then issue another `pop`: `data_out` is zero on the erroneous empty pop, while the reference reads a retained one.

<json>
{
  "lemmas": [
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (size <= DEPTH && size == fv_env.fifo_size); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Reset establishes both occupancies at zero. Their update rules agree for accepted transfers and rejected operations, so the reference occupancy identifies the DUT's occupied entries."
