The lemmas below target `main`’s default `ALLOW_BYPASS=1`, assume `DEPTH >= 1`, and require reset to be sampled at least once. Place them in `main`, where both instances are visible. Assert `lemma_4` for every `k` from `0` through `DEPTH-1` using a generate loop. ([accellera.org](https://accellera.org/images/eda/sv-bc/att-8242/1769_ElaborationTimeUserAssert.080304.pdf?utm_source=openai))

**Limitation:** For `ALLOW_BYPASS=0`, the property is false as written. After filling and draining the FIFO with `1` bits, an additional pop while empty produces `data_out=0`, while the referenced memory bit remains `1`. No sound lemma can prove that case; the property must exclude erroneous pops.

